d view uses the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"centered 220×140 tan card, 888×1212 artboard, and full-bleed framing as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"GitHub macOS runner evidence bound to this head."}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI. One helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami","role":"collection"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/searchable(text:tokens:isPresented:placement:prompt:token:)-7owl5":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"searchable"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"text"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},